  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "Given a rectangle, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the area $S$ if the lengths of sides are $a=4$ and $b=5.$",
  "worked_solution": "The area of the rectangle is $S=ab.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,b) & =(\\frac{\u2202S}{\u2202a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{\u2202S}{\u2202b})\\,\\text{d}b \\\\  & =b\\,\\text{d}a+a\\,\\text{d}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=4$ and $b=5,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(4,5) & =5\\,\\text{d}a+4\\,\\text{d}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
